% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_bunch_item.py` as the GET returns one bunch hydrated. POST updates label, notes, ordered or track_ids, with members rewritten wholesale and position renumbered dense in one transaction. POST {action:'archive'} soft-deletes, leaving activations dangling but restorable; dropping below 2 members auto-archives. A LIBRARY-LEVEL EDIT OR ARCHIVE JOURNALS INTO EVERY PLAN RETURNED BY plan_bunch_activation.plans_activating(bunch_id): otherwise archiving one bunch silently changes the constraints of N plans with no trace in any of their journals. The response reports the affected slugs so the UI can tell the user which other plans it just touched. Because bunch_store cannot journal (it is library-scoped and plan_journal.append requires a slug), this module writes those entries from bunch_store's structured result.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

GET returns one bunch hydrated. POST updates label, notes, ordered or track_ids, with members rewritten wholesale and position renumbered dense in one transaction. POST {action:'archive'} soft-deletes, leaving activations dangling but restorable; dropping below 2 members auto-archives. A LIBRARY-LEVEL EDIT OR ARCHIVE JOURNALS INTO EVERY PLAN RETURNED BY plan_bunch_activation.plans_activating(bunch_id): otherwise archiving one bunch silently changes the constraints of N plans with no trace in any of their journals. The response reports the affected slugs so the UI can tell the user which other plans it just touched. Because bunch_store cannot journal (it is library-scoped and plan_journal.append requires a slug), this module writes those entries from bunch_store's structured result.

